{
  "name": "Multi-Timeframe Trend-Pullback Strategy",
  "raw_text": "Strategy Name: Multi-Timeframe Trend-Pullback Strategy\n\nTimeframes:\n- Bias (4H): overall market direction\n- Trend (1H): confirms bias direction\n- Entry (15m): precise entry trigger\n\nLong Entry Rules:\n1. Bias (4H): 50-period EMA must be sloping upward (current EMA value greater than EMA value 10 bars ago), and price must be trading above the 50-period EMA.\n2. Trend (1H): 20-period EMA must be above the 50-period EMA (bullish EMA alignment).\n3. Entry (15m): price must pull back to touch or cross below the 20-period EMA, then close back above the 20-period EMA on a subsequent candle (pullback-and-reclaim pattern).\n4. RSI (15m, 14-period) must be between 40 and 60 at the moment of entry (avoids entries in overbought/oversold extremes).\n\nShort Entry Rules (mirror of long):\n1. Bias (4H): 50-period EMA sloping downward, price below 50-period EMA.\n2. Trend (1H): 20-period EMA below 50-period EMA (bearish alignment).\n3. Entry (15m): price pulls back to touch or cross above the 20-period EMA, then closes back below it.\n4. RSI (15m, 14-period) between 40 and 60 at entry.\n\nStop Loss:\n- Long: below the low of the pullback candle, minus a 0.2% buffer.\n- Short: above the high of the pullback candle, plus a 0.2% buffer.\n\nTake Profit:\n- Fixed 2.5:1 Risk-Reward ratio.\n\nRisk Management:\n- Risk 1% of account equity per trade, fixed (not compounding).\n\nSession Filters:\n- None specified -- evaluated continuously.",
